# Tests And Quality

- Find the existing scripts before inventing checks. Prefer npm scripts, composer scripts, pytest, xcodebuild, or documented repo commands.
- Run the smallest check that proves the change, then one broader check if the touched area has user-facing or shared behavior.
- For UI changes, use browser verification or screenshots when practical, especially for responsive layout, forms, dashboards, and navigation.
- For bug fixes, add or update a focused regression test when the project has a nearby test pattern.
- Do not update lockfiles unless dependencies actually changed.
- If a check cannot run locally, state exactly why and provide the next best verification performed.
